## Refactor proposal for `src/Card.tsx`

The card is doing three jobs the design system should own: semantics, palette, and layout. Each change below maps to one of the three findings.

### 1. Accessibility — `crime_00001 (accessible_interaction_risk)`

`<div onClick>` on lines 10/22 is unreachable by keyboard and invisible to AT. The fix depends on what "click" means:

- **If it navigates** → render `<a href>`.
- **If it triggers an action** → render `<button type="button">` and let the user reset its default styling.
- **Only if the surrounding element must remain a `<div>`** (e.g. a card-sized hit target with nested interactive children) → add `role="button"`, `tabIndex={0}`, an `aria-label`, and a keyboard handler that mirrors `onClick` on `Enter`/`Space`.

Picking the first form below since the whole card behaves as one target:

```tsx
<button type="button" className={styles.card} onClick={handleActivate} aria-label="Open card">
  …
</button>
```

This also removes the need for a separate `onKeyDown` handler — `<button>` handles Enter/Space natively.

### 2. Design tokens — `crime_00002 (design_token_escape)`

All nine literals on lines 16–20, 24, 27 belong in the theme. Replace inline `style={{ … }}` with semantic class names backed by CSS custom properties, so future agents extending the file inherit the palette rather than copying hex values forward:

```tsx
// src/Card.tsx
import styles from "./Card.module.css";

export function Card({ children, onActivate, label }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <button type="button" className={styles.card} onClick={onActivate} aria-label={label}>
      <div className={styles.body}>{children}</div>
      <aside className={styles.sidebar}>sidebar</aside>
    </button>
  );
}
```

```css
/* src/Card.module.css */
.card {
  background: var(--color-surface-accent);   /* was #ff00aa */
  color: var(--color-text-primary);          /* was #0a0a0a */
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);     /* was #cccccc */
  outline-color: var(--color-focus-ring);    /* was #1a73e8 */
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);              /* was 0 2px 4px rgb(0,0,0) */
  padding: var(--space-6);                   /* was 24 */
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
}
.body    { color: var(--color-text-primary); }   /* was #333333 */
.sidebar { color: var(--color-text-muted); }     /* was #666666 */
```

The hex values now live in `theme.css` (or wherever the project defines `--color-*`). If the project doesn't have tokens yet, this refactor surfaces the gap — but the JSX is already token-shaped, so the swap is a single CSS file when tokens arrive.

### 3. Responsive layout — `crime_00003 (responsive_fragility)`

Lines 12, 24, 27 set hard `width`s of 800/720/240 px; line 24 also pins `fontSize: 18`. None of that survives a 375 px viewport, and there's no `@media` in the file. Fix by driving the layout from intrinsic sizing + a container query, with `clamp()` for type:

```css
.card {
  /* was width: 800; height: 600; maxWidth: 1024 */
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 64rem;
  min-height: 16rem;          /* lets content grow; avoids the fixed 600 */
  container-type: inline-size;

  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 15rem;   /* body + sidebar (was 720 / 240 px) */
  gap: var(--space-4);
}

.body    { font-size: clamp(0.9375rem, 0.85rem + 0.4cqi, 1.125rem); } /* was 18px */
.sidebar { font-size: var(--text-sm); }                                /* was 14px */

@container (max-width: 36rem) {
  .card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }   /* sidebar collapses below body */
}
```

Container query rather than `@media` because a card's responsive behavior should depend on the slot it lives in, not the viewport — that matches the finding's `fix_shape: "drive layout from container queries or a fluid scale, not pixel media queries"`.

### Mapping summary

| Finding | Change |
|---|---|
| `accessible_interaction_risk` | Root element becomes `<button type="button">` with `aria-label`; click handler lifted to a named prop. |
| `design_token_escape` | All nine literals moved to `Card.module.css` and bound to `var(--color-*)`, `var(--space-*)`, `var(--shadow-*)`. |
| `responsive_fragility` | Fixed `width`/`fontSize` replaced with `max-width` + `grid-template-columns`, `clamp()` typography, and a `@container` rule that collapses the sidebar. |

After applying, `crimes scan src/Card.tsx` should drop all three findings; the file becomes a thin JSX shell over a token-driven, container-responsive stylesheet with a keyboard-reachable activation target.
